    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0229" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/4–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-05T19:00:00-04:00">April 5, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2662. Substance of Department’s 2577, April 3, 8 p.m.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d172-f1"/> and a copy of your 3405, April 4, noon were communicated
                    to the President. In reply he has sent the following directive: “I do not wish
                    any document or proposal changing the unconditional surrender terms”.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
